{"game": "deep-rock-galactic", "language": "english", "appid": 548430, "month": "2026-07", "window": 2, "start_date": 1783555200, "end_date": 1784159999, "month_true_total": 678, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-08-29 21:30:29 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "230563417", "author": {"steamid": "76561199055815257", "personaname": "ChoportXGaming", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199055815257/", "num_games_owned": 227, "num_reviews": 53, "playtime_forever": 161, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 161, "last_played": 1778353348, "avatar": "c8b892e47942cef8b574b661630441521a52c4b2"}, "language": "english", "review": "It’s good, but at the same time, it’s just... not.\nDeep Rock Galactic is a weird one for me. Objectively, I can see why people love it. Digging for minerals, shooting alien bugs, and playing as space dwarves is a unique concept, and the game is mechanically very well-made.\n\nBut at the same time, it just doesn't fully click. After a few missions, the core gameplay loop of \"drop in, mine, fight off waves, and escape\" started to feel incredibly repetitive. If you aren't playing with a dedicated group of friends, the magic wears off almost instantly.\n\nIt has its fun moments, but then it quickly falls back into feeling like a chore. It is a decent game, but it's missing whatever spark is needed to actually make me want to keep playing it.\n\n5/10 — Rock and Stone, I guess? It's okay, but it is definitely not for everyone.", "timestamp_created": 1784151605, "timestamp_updated": 1784151605, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1519804887", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "230553063", "author": {"steamid": "76561199206432660",